WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:01.720
Yeah, go ahead.

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:04.609
I just wanted to get clean audio on you saying
no boners in sight.

00:00:04.609 --> 00:00:10.130
That was all I wanted, Brian.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:14.450
How could Loki affect phase four?

00:00:14.450 --> 00:00:16.810
How could it not affect phase four, Brian?

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:17.850
That's my question.

00:00:17.850 --> 00:00:19.410
I don't know.

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:21.070
I'm excited to find out.

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:25.090
It seems clear that right now Marvel's really
leaning into the whole multi-verse thing so

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:32.250
that's going to be fascinating to watch and
see how long audiences want to keep watching

00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:33.829
that happen over and over again.

00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:34.929
I don't know.

00:00:34.929 --> 00:00:37.859
Things have gotten-
I'm interested to find out.

00:00:37.859 --> 00:00:41.570
-extremely weird in a very short span of time.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:42.570
Yeah.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:43.570
Yeah.

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:47.211
Just where the introduction of the multi-verse
in Loki was just kind of like, okay, this

00:00:47.211 --> 00:00:50.210
is happening now and everyone seems to be
on board.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:52.420
Everyone's just like, "Okay, multi-verse.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:53.420
Alligator.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.420
Got it.

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:55.420
Yes.

00:00:55.420 --> 00:00:56.420
Next."

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:59.609
And it's pretty interesting, and it'll be
interesting to see how long they are able

00:00:59.609 --> 00:01:03.899
to maintain that interest in a very-
Wasn't it a crocodile?

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:04.899
Crocodile?

00:01:04.899 --> 00:01:06.360
Was it an alligator? I don't know.

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:07.524
It was an alligator, Nina.

00:01:07.524 --> 00:01:10.460
It was some kind of-
I thought people were calling him Croki, like

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:11.460
crocodile Loki?

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:14.890
I mean, they were, that doesn't necessarily
mean that they're right.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:15.890
That's true.

00:01:15.890 --> 00:01:17.660
It's not like there's a lot of zoologists
in the MCU probably.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:18.660
Right?

00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:21.920
Don't turtles technically have fins and tortoises
have feet?

00:01:21.920 --> 00:01:22.920
I don't know.

00:01:22.920 --> 00:01:24.510
I don't know anything about anything in the
animal kingdom.

00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:26.900
I think they're thinking of flippers, Brian,
you're thinking of flippers.

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:27.900
What did I say?

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:28.400
Fins?

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:31.493
Just before the turtle gang goes crazy in
the comment section.

00:01:31.493 --> 00:01:32.634
Let me tell you all.

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:34.164
The turtle stans, yeah.

00:01:34.284 --> 00:01:35.720
You know what I meant.

00:01:35.720 --> 00:01:36.720
Be careful.

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:41.060
We've been doing this for literally two minutes
and we're already extremely off topic.

00:01:41.060 --> 00:01:42.920
Arguing about turtles.

00:01:42.920 --> 00:01:46.381
Just like every other episode.

00:01:46.381 --> 00:01:52.580
How do we think it's going to affect the MCU
specifically, Tom?

00:01:52.580 --> 00:01:58.330
So, like I said, I'm interested to see how
long we want to put up with, not put up with,

00:01:58.330 --> 00:02:00.970
how long it's going to stay enjoyable before
people get bored with it?

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:06.380
Because it sounds like there are, we have
at least three projects coming up that are

00:02:06.380 --> 00:02:09.869
based pretty firmly in the multi-verse from
what anybody can tell?

00:02:09.869 --> 00:02:13.110
We have Dr. Strange in the Multi-Verse of
Madness, that's the title.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:14.900
Kind of gives the game away.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.400
Then you've got the new Spider-Man movie that
I feel like everybody like tried to keep it

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.930
very quiet then Alfred Molina showed up.

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:22.721
He was like, "Oh yeah, I'm doing it.

00:02:22.721 --> 00:02:23.823
I'm back.

00:02:23.823 --> 00:02:26.299
Great to be back in the arms after 20 years.

00:02:26.299 --> 00:02:27.560
Good to see everybody."

00:02:27.560 --> 00:02:30.319
And then Ant-Man 3, Quantumania.

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:32.099
Which we know Kang will be in.

00:02:32.099 --> 00:02:33.099
Right.

00:02:33.099 --> 00:02:38.340
Because that was when they first announced
the amazing Jonathan Majors, who I loved in

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:42.939
the Loki finale, he was perfect, will be a
part of the film.

00:02:42.939 --> 00:02:47.200
And that's the other thing that I'm really
interested to see what they do with it because

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:52.060
Kang as a character in the comics never really
did anything for me, not my all-time favorite.

00:02:52.060 --> 00:02:59.650
He always just seemed too convoluted and stupid,
I said it, I don't care.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.209
Kang the Conqueror was stupid.

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:06.099
I mean, knowing what you know about Kang,
and we'll try to fill in the blanks for each

00:03:06.099 --> 00:03:10.349
other, what can you tell us about the origins
of Kang the Conqueror as a character?

00:03:10.349 --> 00:03:11.500
I would be happy to.

00:03:11.500 --> 00:03:12.500
Okay.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:16.220
We begin our story in the 31st century, a
young man named Nathaniel Richards gets bored

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:23.200
and decides that he wants to stop living in
a futuristic utopia and instead go be a Pharaoh

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.200
for awhile.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:25.200
So he time travels.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.239
He time travels right back to-
So relatable.

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:28.239
Yeah.

00:03:28.239 --> 00:03:29.239
We've all been there.

00:03:29.239 --> 00:03:30.239
Yeah.

00:03:30.239 --> 00:03:31.239
If I had a nickel.

00:03:31.239 --> 00:03:34.019
Quarantine had a lot of us kind of exploring
our options.

00:03:34.019 --> 00:03:36.010
So he does that.

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:38.269
He gets beat up for awhile.

00:03:38.269 --> 00:03:39.269
After that, it gets kind of fuzzy.

00:03:39.269 --> 00:03:41.540
He travels back into the future.

00:03:41.540 --> 00:03:42.779
He meets a girl.

00:03:42.779 --> 00:03:48.290
He can't take over the 20th century because
there are too many Hulks and Ironmen.

00:03:48.290 --> 00:03:51.450
He tries to impress a girl by, by beating
up the Avengers.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.799
The girl dies.

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:57.640
Then there are a ton of different multi-versal
Kangs and time-travel

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:59.480
Kings and all of these.

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.059
I was just never on board with whatever his
master plan was.

00:04:02.059 --> 00:04:06.000
He's like a confusing, time traveling Dr.
Doom.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.000
Very much.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.000
Yeah.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:09.489
Just minus like a lot of the super powers.

00:04:09.489 --> 00:04:10.489
Right.

00:04:10.489 --> 00:04:11.489
And the cool name.

00:04:11.489 --> 00:04:12.900
Kang the Conqueror, just not a great name.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:13.900
No.

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:18.620
That being said, Thanos, I was never super
stoked for him in the comics either and then

00:04:18.620 --> 00:04:21.530
they turned him into this really compelling
character and it kind of looks like what they're

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.569
doing with Kang and I hope they pull it off.

00:04:23.569 --> 00:04:24.569
Yeah.

00:04:24.569 --> 00:04:28.009
Nina, you, you mentioned something about how
good you thought Jonathan Majors was in the

00:04:28.009 --> 00:04:29.009
Loki finale.

00:04:29.009 --> 00:04:30.009
Yeah.

00:04:30.009 --> 00:04:31.009
I agree.

00:04:31.009 --> 00:04:33.570
Do you want to tell us what you thought generally
about that performance and what you think

00:04:33.570 --> 00:04:36.360
it promises for the future of the MCU?

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:45.744
Well, now that I know that Kang is maybe not
the greatest comic book character, according

00:04:45.744 --> 00:04:47.503
to one Tom.

00:04:47.503 --> 00:04:48.972
One Tom.

00:04:48.972 --> 00:04:50.216
A singular Tom.

00:04:50.216 --> 00:04:51.218
Me too.

00:04:51.218 --> 00:04:52.699
I'll throw in-
One white man in his 30s.

00:04:52.699 --> 00:04:56.630
No, but now that I know that he's maybe not
the most attention grabbing villain I think

00:04:56.630 --> 00:05:01.379
it's perfect to cast a really, really compelling
actor like Majors.

00:05:01.379 --> 00:05:09.080
I mean, the finale aired one day after he
got his Emmy nomination for Lovecraft Country,

00:05:09.080 --> 00:05:11.009
which was canceled.

00:05:11.009 --> 00:05:16.090
Very weird move, but he really lights up the
screen in everything that he does.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:18.770
He's definitely an actor to watch.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:25.990
And I mean, with the right casting and the
right writing and working with directors like,

00:05:25.990 --> 00:05:29.960
Peyton Reed will be doing the third Ant-Man
and all of these people who we know are really...

00:05:29.960 --> 00:05:31.949
Do we know who's directing Dr. Strange 2?

00:05:31.949 --> 00:05:33.110
It is slipping my mind.

00:05:33.110 --> 00:05:34.539
Sam Raimi.

00:05:34.539 --> 00:05:36.110
That's right! So, yeah.

00:05:36.110 --> 00:05:37.928
He's got Sam Raimi. Thank you.

00:05:37.928 --> 00:05:39.907
So yeah, he's going to work with Sam Raimi.

00:05:39.907 --> 00:05:43.718
I have every faith that he's going to be,
he's got a great creative team behind him

00:05:43.718 --> 00:05:46.960
and I also think that Majors is going to keep
bringing it in his performance.

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:49.960
Because I just loved like the, "Really?

00:05:49.960 --> 00:05:53.810
Who cares," attitude he brought to the character.

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:58.070
I love when there's like a super high-stakes
situation, the person's like, "Oh, whatever."

00:05:58.070 --> 00:05:59.750
He was having a really good time.

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:01.010
He was having a great time.

00:06:01.010 --> 00:06:02.880
He chewed every piece of scenery into shreds.

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.473
I loved it.

00:06:04.473 --> 00:06:07.340
And I just think that's the right attitude
for a Marvel villain.

00:06:07.340 --> 00:06:09.550
I mean, that's why Kathryn Hahn was so good.

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:12.720
That's why Cate Blanchett was so good in Thor
Ragnarok.

00:06:12.720 --> 00:06:17.250
Chew the scenery and really give it 150% and
you're going to be a good Marvel villain.

00:06:17.250 --> 00:06:18.699
So I think he's going to be great.

00:06:18.699 --> 00:06:24.070
And just from an acting perspective, I think
that it could be a really cool part to play.

00:06:24.070 --> 00:06:25.070
Yeah.

00:06:25.070 --> 00:06:28.960
From what they've given us so far, like there
are going to be these infinite different variations

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:29.960
of a character.

00:06:29.960 --> 00:06:30.960
Yes.

00:06:30.960 --> 00:06:32.870
So it could be a great-
So he's going to have a lot of stuff to do.

00:06:32.870 --> 00:06:33.870
Yeah.

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:34.870
Yeah.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:36.461
This really cool showcase for his talents.

00:06:36.461 --> 00:06:37.461
Yeah, absolutely.

00:06:37.461 --> 00:06:39.298
That'll be neat to watch, I hope.

00:06:39.298 --> 00:06:44.129
That was what I was going to say in terms
of you're going to get Kang in Ant-Man and

00:06:44.129 --> 00:06:48.440
The Wasp Quantumania, and we're going to see
one interpretation of this character.

00:06:48.440 --> 00:06:53.870
And then we're going to get probably again
in Dr. Strange in the Multi-verse of Madness

00:06:53.870 --> 00:07:00.621
or one is first and then the other comes later,
I don't quite remember the order, but there's

00:07:00.621 --> 00:07:04.530
a potential to see this character in every
one of these movies in some form or another,

00:07:04.530 --> 00:07:06.660
like an end of movie stinger.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:10.769
And you're not going to know which version
you're seeing, you know what I mean?

00:07:10.769 --> 00:07:11.851
Right.

00:07:11.851 --> 00:07:16.860
That's what's so potentially exciting about
it, which is will he be four or five different

00:07:16.860 --> 00:07:17.860
Kangs in Ant-Man?

00:07:17.860 --> 00:07:18.860
Right.

00:07:18.860 --> 00:07:20.969
I don't know, but he might be six or seven
or eight in all the other movies, too.

00:07:20.969 --> 00:07:25.509
And with an actor who, in this he was very
funny, and he's really serious in Lovecraft

00:07:25.509 --> 00:07:31.840
Country, but somebody who can play both sides
of the coin, I think the role's in very good

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:32.840
hands.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:33.840
Yeah.

00:07:33.840 --> 00:07:34.840
I think it's going to be really cool.

00:07:34.840 --> 00:07:39.360
And I'm excited that they didn't take that
long to give us our new Thanos.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:44.319
When Thanos first got teased in the original
Marvel movies, the first Avengers was when

00:07:44.319 --> 00:07:48.520
we first saw him, obviously everyone, all
fans were like, "Oh, Thanos is coming.

00:07:48.520 --> 00:07:49.520
I know Thanos.

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:50.699
I recognize him."

00:07:50.699 --> 00:07:57.729
But as Tom was saying, it's not as though,
with some exceptions, I'm sure most people

00:07:57.729 --> 00:08:02.479
don't think of Thanos and go, "Oh, I really
like how he, you know?"

00:08:02.479 --> 00:08:05.129
He's just a big purple guy.

00:08:05.129 --> 00:08:06.910
Great, big, strong purple guy.

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:07.910
Doesn't like people around.

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:08.910
He likes having a shiny glove.

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:09.910
Yeah.

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:10.910
He's in love with death.

00:08:10.910 --> 00:08:12.300
That was his big thing.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:17.069
He's very into equity, but that gets overlooked.

00:08:17.069 --> 00:08:18.069
Yeah.

00:08:18.069 --> 00:08:24.249
Anyway, what I like about it was they set
it up in a way that left a lot to your imagination.

00:08:24.249 --> 00:08:27.439
And then once they figured it out, they started
going in that direction.

00:08:27.439 --> 00:08:28.439
Yeah.

00:08:28.439 --> 00:08:30.270
But here I feel like they've got it figured
out from the outset.

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:34.600
So Kang is a particular kind of guy in a particular
kind of way.

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:38.990
And even though we're going to see different
versions of him, probably, in all these different

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:44.210
movies and shows, I feel like they're starting
off on really solid footing.

00:08:44.210 --> 00:08:45.560
That has me really excited.

00:08:45.560 --> 00:08:46.560
Well.

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:50.420
And to piggyback off of that, in terms of
how it's going to affect phase four, I think

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:56.020
everybody was like, "What is going to be the
next crossover thing now there's not more

00:08:56.020 --> 00:08:57.020
Avengers?

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:58.020
Exactly.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:03.160
That's going to bring everybody together and
create a multi-movie conflict, even with letting

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:09.200
some things stand alone because as we discussed
today, looking over the phase four list, some

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:11.100
things you're like, "Kang will be in that.

00:09:11.100 --> 00:09:12.100
This will have to do with this story."

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:13.860
And then other things you're like, "Probably
not.

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:16.230
That's probably not going to be related."

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:18.519
I had a thought about that.

00:09:18.519 --> 00:09:23.190
I have a thought about how they're going to
incorporate Kang and the multi-verse into

00:09:23.190 --> 00:09:27.457
all these movies that wouldn't seemingly have
anything to do with it, like-

00:09:27.457 --> 00:09:28.707
Is it Photoshop?

00:09:28.707 --> 00:09:29.707
-Shang-Chi.

00:09:29.707 --> 00:09:30.932
Well, you're not too far off.

00:09:30.932 --> 00:09:36.240
You know how sometimes in a movie you'll be
filming one thing and then there's a guy in

00:09:36.240 --> 00:09:39.274
the background and then they cut to someone
else and then they cut back and the guy's

00:09:39.274 --> 00:09:40.274
gone.

00:09:40.417 --> 00:09:42.110
Or there's different paths.

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:44.230
And you think they're just going to put Kang
in the background of everything?

00:09:44.230 --> 00:09:45.820
I mean, something like that.

00:09:45.820 --> 00:09:51.040
I think they might start to introduce some
interesting continuity errors that are-

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:52.959
Oh!
-a bit more noticeable.

00:09:52.959 --> 00:09:54.240
That is cool, actually.

00:09:54.240 --> 00:09:56.120
And people will be like, "Oh, look at this
mistake.

00:09:56.120 --> 00:09:57.790
Look at that mistake."

00:09:57.790 --> 00:10:01.180
And then in one in one of these movies you're
going to have like this flashback.

00:10:01.180 --> 00:10:07.500
So all the times things were subtly changing
and that's characters hopping dimensions,

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:08.920
hopping timelines.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:12.340
I never watched any of these shows because
I enjoy sleeping at night, but I've written

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:15.540
about enough of them, The like Haunting of
Hill house, Haunting of Bly Manor, all the

00:10:15.540 --> 00:10:20.670
ghost hunting people did and the frames where
it was like there was a ghost in almost every

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:21.970
frame of the show or something.

00:10:21.970 --> 00:10:22.970
That's awesome.

00:10:22.970 --> 00:10:24.639
And people had to keep finding them.

00:10:24.639 --> 00:10:28.160
Again, I would rather pluck my eyes from my
skull than watch that.

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:29.160
No offense.

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:30.160
I'm such a wimp.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:31.420
None taken.

00:10:31.420 --> 00:10:32.420
I can't do it.

00:10:32.420 --> 00:10:33.420
I just can't.

00:10:33.420 --> 00:10:34.420
I would never sleep.

00:10:34.420 --> 00:10:35.440
No one's asking you to.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:36.440
It's okay.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:37.440
Don't pluck your eyes out.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:38.440
Fine!

00:10:38.440 --> 00:10:39.691
I work for a pop culture website.

00:10:39.691 --> 00:10:40.820
I feel pressure.

00:10:40.820 --> 00:10:41.870
It's okay.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:42.870
It's all right.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:48.320
I think you're onto something really cool
there though, that intentional errors will

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:49.610
end up forming the backbone.

00:10:49.610 --> 00:10:50.790
I kind of love that.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:51.790
Continuity errors.

00:10:51.790 --> 00:10:57.370
I hope they do that because that'll be a funny-
Like one scene In No Way Home, Ned will be

00:10:57.370 --> 00:11:01.190
there wearing a Hawaiian shirt that's blue
and then they'll cut to Peter Parker and then

00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:04.820
they'll cut back and he's wearing a Hawaiian
shirt that's red, and no one will say anything,

00:11:04.820 --> 00:11:06.580
And we'll all just be like, "Huh?

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:07.580
What?"

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:10.110
And it'll be little things.

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:12.040
And then as time goes on, this is in my head,
this is what's going to happen.

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:13.040
I love it.

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:15.290
So that's how I think it could affect everything.

00:11:15.290 --> 00:11:16.980
Tom looks really excited about this.

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:20.290
You know what I would love so much.

